  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Alabama has received $15.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The federal government awarded 92,145 contracts in that period, with an average award size of $171K. Obligations fell 13.0% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $10.3B, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $2.8B. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and THE BOEING COMPANY each received $1.3B, and DYNETICS, INC. received $1.1B. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations at $4.2B, with Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing second at $2.7B. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Engineering Services also rank in the top industries with $1B and $1.4B respectively. These figures reflect fiscal year to date totals and are partial for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Alabama changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations in Alabama fell 13.0% year over year. Fiscal-year totals show growth from $13.1B in FY21 to $18.1B in FY25, then $15.8B in FY26 to date. The Department of Defense remains the dominant buyer with $10.3B in obligations for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest industries and vendors in Alabama federal contracting?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) leads industries with $4.2B in obligations. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and THE BOEING COMPANY top vendors with $1.3B each, and DYNETICS, INC. follows with $1.1B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $2.7B, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $1B."
      }
    ]
  },
